[16.08302, "o", "3:Mixed investigation briefs, committee minutes, mail excerpts, policy exceptions, correction notices, and ledger rows. Extractor policy is distributed across the file.\r\n7:This index orients readers only. Binding reconciliation rules appear inside Investigation Briefs 01–08 and the Mid-Year Amendment in Brief 09. Draft narrative, decoy sections, and archived threads are not authoritative. Structured source data appears near the file end under Email Excerpts, Policy Exceptions, Correction Notices, and the canonical Transaction Ledger heading.\r\n11:## Investigation Brief 01 — Ledger Sourcing\r\n17:line is exactly `## Transaction Ledger` as authoritative. The archive also\r\n28:## Investigation Brief 01 — Ledger Sourcing — field notes\r\n257:amendments, and corrections. Ledger rows provide the base status (lowercase on\r\n477:after ledger rows, meeting amendments, and mail excerpts have been merged.\r\n685:## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice Precedence\r\n696:## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notic"]
[16.083078, "o", "e Precedence — field notes\r\n832:Committee minutes show owner churn from unsigned drafts. Ledger owner is the\r\n1063:ledger `date` field (YYYY-MM-DD on output). When a winning correction notice\r\n1677:ledger date immediately before correction notices are applied — that is, the date\r\n1679:before any correction notice changes `date` or `status`. Brief 03 still governs\r\n3866:## Correction Notices\r\n3904:## Transaction Ledger (working copy)\r\n3912:## Transaction Ledger\r\n"]
